{"count":1088,"next":"https://api.afp.mil.ph/articles/?page=5&page_size=100","previous":"https://api.afp.mil.ph/articles/?page=3&page_size=100","results":[{"id":513,"title":"TDCSAFP welcomes US Congressional Staff Members ","slug":"tdcsafp-welcomes-us-congressional-staff-members","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City- MGen Ferdinand Barandon, Acting Deputy Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (TDCSAFP), welcomed US Congressional Staff Members, during a courtesy visit on April 22, 2024, at AFP Commissioned Officers’ Country, Camp General Emilio Aguinaldo.  </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/April%202024/CS%201.jpg","image_caption":"MGen Barandon, Acting TDCSAFP, AFP Officers, and US Congressional Staff Members, gather for a photo opportunity during the latter’s courtesy visit on April 22, 2024, at AFP Commissioned Officers’ Country, Camp General Emilio Aguinaldo.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-04-22T10:53:12+08:00","hits":2289},{"id":514,"title":"VCSAFP welcomes U.S. Marine Corps Forces Pacific Commander to the AFP","slug":"vcsafp-welcomes-u-s-marine-corps-forces-pacific-commander-to-the-afp","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City- LtGen Arthur Cordura, Vice Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (VCSAFP), welcomed LtGen William Jurney, Commander of U.S. Marine Corps Forces Pacific (MARFORPAC), during his courtesy visit on April 22, 2024, at AFP General Headquarters.  </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Central to the discussion was the upcoming Balikatan 2024 exercises, a cornerstone of the PH-US civic and military cooperation. In their meeting, the two parties reaffirmed their longstanding alliance, highlighting the importance of collaborative efforts in addressing complexities brought by ever-evolving regional security challenges.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/April%202024/SA%201.jpg","image_caption":"LtGen Arthur Cordura, Vice Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (VCSAFP), receives a token of appreciation from LtGen William Jurney, Commander of U.S. Marine Corps Forces Pacific (MARFORPAC), during the latter’s courtesy visit on April 22, 2024 at AFP General Headquarters.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-04-22T10:51:42+08:00","hits":1452},{"id":515,"title":"PH-US strengthen alliance as Exercise Balikatan 2024 begins","slug":"ph-us-strengthen-alliance-as-exercise-balikatan-2024-begins","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) and the United States military are officially underway with Exercise Balikatan 2024, as the annual bilateral exercise kicked off today, April 22, here.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The opening ceremony was distinguished by the presence of United States (US) Embassy Chargé d’ Affaires a.i. Robert Ewing as the Guest of Honor and Speaker representing the US Ambassador to the Philippines, Her Excellency Marykay Loss Carlson, alongside AFP Chief of Staff, General Romeo S Brawner Jr.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/April%202024/OC2.jpg","image_caption":"United States (US) Embassy Chargé d’ Affaires a.i. Robert Ewing together with AFP Chief of Staff, General Romeo S. Brawner Jr link arms to symbolize the essence of \"Balikatan\" during the Opening Ceremony on April 22, 2024 at AFPCOC, Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-04-22T07:49:09+08:00","hits":1801},{"id":516,"title":"AFP Chief congratulates Zamboanga del Sur’s 3rd year as insurgency-free province","slug":"afp-chief-congratulates-zamboanga-del-sur-s-3rd-year-as-insurgency-free-province","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) Chief of Staff General Romeo S Brawner Jr. joined the celebration of the 3rd anniversary of Zamboanga del Sur's declaration as an insurgency-free province at the Provincial Government Center, Barangay Dao, Pagadian City, on Sunday, April 21. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/April%202024/ZAMB%201.jpg","image_caption":"AFP Chief of Staff General Romeo S Brawner Jr with OPAPRU Secretary Carlito Galvez, Zamboanga del Sur Governor Victor Yu and other members of the provincial government and military members joined by former rebels released white doves as a symbol of peace after the ceremony on April 21 in Pagadian City. (Photo by SSg Ambay)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-04-21T15:50:20+08:00","hits":1468},{"id":517,"title":"AFPRESCOM Inaugurates Modernized Training Infrastructure","slug":"afprescom-inaugurates-modernized-training-infrastructure","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City- Brigadier General Vicente Ronatay, Commander of the Armed Forces of the Philippines Reserve Command (AFPRESCOM), led the inauguration ceremony of a newly constructed training school building on April 19, 2024. The event marks a significant step in AFPRESCOM's efforts to modernize its training facilities.</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/April%202024/inf%201.jpg","image_caption":"Brigadier General Ronatay, Commander AFPRESCOM, and Senator Mark Villar during the ceremonial ribbon-cutting to mark the newly-constructed AFPRESCOM training school building on April 19, 2024.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-04-19T15:47:15+08:00","hits":1405},{"id":518,"title":"AFP Chief lauds CRSAFP for advancing national defense strategy","slug":"afp-chief-lauds-crsafp-for-advancing-national-defense-strategy","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City- LtGen Arthur Cordura, Acting Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines representing Gen Romeo Brawner Jr., (CSAFP), acknowledged the dedication of Civil Relations Service Armed Forces of the Philippines (CRSAFP) in promoting the nation’s security architecture during its 73rd founding anniversary on April 18, 2024.</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/April%202024/CRSAFOA2.jpg","image_caption":"LtGen Arthur Cordura, Acting CSAFP, along with MGen Zagala, Commander, CRSAFP, and CRSAFP Personnel pose for a photo opportunity at the CRSAFP 73rd founding anniversary on April 18, 2024.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-04-18T10:09:00+08:00","hits":1819},{"id":519,"title":"AFPCES, FEO, and ASCI Partnership: expect financial packages for Philippine firearms and ammunition","slug":"afpces-feo-and-asci-partnership-expect-financial-packages-for-philippine-firearms-and-ammunition","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City- Armed Forces of the Philippines Commissary, Exchange Services (AFPCES), Firearms Explosive Office (FEO), and Armscor Shooting Center Inc (ASCI) Partnership marks a significant pursuit in providing financial packages of Philippine firearms and ammunition during its launching at AFPCOC, CGEA on April 16, 2024.</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/April%202024/ARMS2.jpg","image_caption":"LtGen Steve Crespillo presented as Acting TDCSAFP along with Captain Ferdinand Gloria, Commander of AFPCES, and partners gathered for a photo opportunity at the launching of AFPCES, FEO, and ASCI Partnership on April 16, 2024.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-04-18T10:06:47+08:00","hits":1522},{"id":520,"title":"PH-US Balikatan Exercise 2024 Set to Commence","slug":"ph-us-balikatan-exercise-2024-set-to-commence","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) and the United States military are gearing up for Balikatan 2024, marking the 39th iteration of the annual bilateral exercise. Scheduled to unfold across Luzon from April 22 to May 10, the event will see more than 16,000 service members from both nations converge for joint training.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">This year’s Balikatan aims to bolster collaboration and readiness across a spectrum of critical areas including external defense operations, cyber defense, counterterrorism, humanitarian assistance and disaster response, and interagency capacity-building. This robust engagement underscores the enduring partnership between the two nations and their shared commitment to regional security and stability.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/April%202024/BK39-24%20Logo.png","image_caption":"Exercise Balikatan 39-24","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-04-16T07:44:57+08:00","hits":4618},{"id":521,"title":"AFP Chief of Staff commends SOCOM troop members for their unwavering commitment to service","slug":"afp-chief-of-staff-commends-socom-troop-members-for-their-unwavering-commitment-to-service","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (CSAFP), General Romeo S Brawner Jr., encouraged AFP Special Operations Command (SOCOM) to maintain their dedication as the primary special force operator during the AFPSOCOM 6th Founding Anniversary at Fort Magsaysay, Nueva Ecija on Monday, April 15, 2024.</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/April%202024/SOLC1.jpg","image_caption":"The Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (CSAFP), General Romeo S Brawner Jr., pay homage by laying wreaths during the 6th Founding Anniversary of the AFP Special Operations Command (SOCOM) at Fort Magsaysay, Nueva Ecija on Monday, April 15, 2024.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-04-15T15:44:32+08:00","hits":1252},{"id":522,"title":"CSAFP visits, condoles with families of fallen navy pilots","slug":"csafp-visits-condoles-with-families-of-fallen-navy-pilots","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City -- The Chief of Staff, Armed Forces of the Philippines (CSAFP), General Romeo S Brawner Jr, visited the wake of Lieutenant Jan Kyle Borres and Ensign Izzah Taccad at the Libingan ng mga Bayani, Taguig City on April 12.</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/April%202024/pnk%201.jpg","image_caption":"General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, pays his respects to one of the two navy aviators who died in a plane crash in Cavite.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-04-14T11:29:09+08:00","hits":758},{"id":523,"title":"CSAFP urges senior enlisted leaders: adjust to present challenges","slug":"csafp-urges-senior-enlisted-leaders-adjust-to-present-challenges","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City - General Romeo Brawner Jr., Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (CSAFP), urged senior enlisted leaders of the military to adjust to present day challenges during the closing ceremony of Senior Enlisted Leaders Forum 2024 in Palawan on April 12, 2024.</span></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">The forum gathered the AFP's different sergeants major to elicit policy recommendations pertaining to the training, morale and welfare, troop discipline and other matters concerning the enlisted personnel of the AFP.","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/April%202024/SLF.jpg","image_caption":"Senior Enlisted Leaders, along with General Romeo Brawner Jr., Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (CSAFP) gather for a photo opportunity at the closing ceremony of the Senior Enlisted Leaders Forum 2024 in Palawan on April 12, 2024.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-04-12T11:25:06+08:00","hits":794},{"id":524,"title":"AFP joins Commemoration of 82nd Day of Valor","slug":"afp-joins-commemoration-of-82nd-day-of-valor","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) joined the nation in honoring the 82nd Anniversary of Araw ng Kagitingan (Day of Valor) at Mt. Samat National Shrine in Pilar, Bataan on Tuesday, April 9, 2024.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">General Romeo S Brawner Jr, attended the ceremony led by President Ferdinand R. Marcos Jr. Under the theme 'Honoring Veterans' Valor: Foundation for a United Filipino People,' the commemoration signified a solemn tribute to the unwavering courage and sacrifices of our veterans, whose valor serves as the foundation for a united Filipino people. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/April%202024/ak24.jpg","image_caption":"President Ferdinand R. Marcos Jr., together with United States of America (USA) Charge d'Affaires Robert Ewing (left) and Ambassador Endo Kazuya of Japan (right), pay their homage by laying wreaths at the historic monument during the 82nd Day of Valor in Mt. Samat National Shrine in Pilar, Bataan on Tuesday, April 9. Behind them is AFP Chief of Staff, General Romeo S Brawner Jr.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-04-09T14:20:04+08:00","hits":807},{"id":525,"title":"AFP STATEMENT | On the Commemoration of Araw ng Kagitingan","slug":"afp-statement-on-the-commemoration-of-araw-ng-kagitingan","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/April%202024/AKMES.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-04-09T14:15:55+08:00","hits":652},{"id":526,"title":"CSAFP presides over donning of ranks ceremony for Senator Miguel Zubiri","slug":"csafp-presides-over-donning-of-ranks-ceremony-for-senator-miguel-zubiri","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City-General Romeo Brawner Jr., Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (CSAFP), led the ceremony to don military ranks to Philippine Senate President Juan Miguel Zubiri on April 8, 2024.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Senator Zubiri was conferred with the minimum rank of Lieutenant Colonel, in accordance with Republic Act 7077 Section 44, which permits elected officials and presidential appointees to be commissioned in the Reserve Force subject to existing AFP rules and regulations. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/April%202024/Z.jpg","image_caption":"Senate President Juan Miguel Zubiri, is being donned new ranks by General Romeo Brawner Jr., Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, and Ms Audrey Tan-Zubiri on April 8 in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.  Photo by TSg Obinque/PAOAFP","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-04-08T14:08:16+08:00","hits":1009},{"id":527,"title":"Philippines, United States, Australia and Japan hold first Multilateral Maritime Cooperative Activity in West Philippine Sea","slug":"philippines-united-states-australia-and-japan-hold-first-multilateral-maritime-cooperative-activity-in-west-philippine-sea","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP), United States Indo-Pacific Command (USINDOPACOM), Australian Defence Force (ADF) and Japan Self-Defense Forces (JSDF) successfully conducted the first Multilateral Maritime Cooperative Activity (MMCA) in the West Philippine Sea on Sunday, April 7. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/April%202024/MCAAPR%201.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-04-07T09:22:34+08:00","hits":2606},{"id":528,"title":"AFP Hosts Pre-Sail Briefing for Historic Multilateral Maritime Cooperative Activity","slug":"afp-hosts-pre-sail-briefing-for-historic-multilateral-maritime-cooperative-activity","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) hosted a pre-sail conference for the inaugural Multilateral Maritime Cooperative Activity (MCA) on Saturday, April 6. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Key planning members from the AFP, Australian Defence Force, Japan Self Defense Force, and United States Indo-Pacific Command convened at the Headquarters, Western Command in Puerto Princesa, to finalize plans for this historic activity. Scheduled within the Philippine Exclusive Economic Zone, the MCA underscores the commitment to uphold international law while promoting peace and stability in the region.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/April%202024/pres%201.jpg","image_caption":"Navy Captain Brix Dumanig, WESCOM’s Assistant Chief of Unified Command Staff for Operations discuss pre-sail plans with USS Mobile LCS26 Skipper Commander David Gardner and Royal Australian Navy HMAS Warramunga Commanding Officer Commander Jennifer Graham at the Western Command Headquarters in Puerto Princesa City on April 6.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-04-06T09:19:11+08:00","hits":867},{"id":529,"title":"AFP, US military elevate partnership through first Information Warfighter Exercise ","slug":"afp-us-military-elevate-partnership-through-first-information-warfighter-exercise","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines and the United States military successfully completed the inaugural Information Warfighter Exercise (IWX) from April 1 to 5, here at the General Headquarters. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The week-long exercise strengthened interoperability between AFP and US information operations planners, empowered the AFP with enhanced IO capabilities, and set the standard for future local IO training programs. Key law enforcement agencies such as the Philippine National Police and the Philippine Coast Guard, actively engaged in the exercise, emphasizing its comprehensive scope and significance in strengthening national defense strategies.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/April%202024/IWX%201.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-04-06T09:16:01+08:00","hits":994},{"id":530,"title":"Gen Brawner Jr, US Sec Kendall discuss PH-US military alliance","slug":"gen-brawner-jr-us-sec-kendall-discuss-ph-us-military-alliance","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, and United States Secretary of the Air Force Frank Kendall discussed Philippine-United States military alliance during the latter’s courtesy visit on April 5 to the AFP General Headquarters here.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The two affirmed the continuation of military engagements and cooperative work, including maritime cooperative activity, bilateral exercises, and EDCA sites projects, as a message to the world of the ironclad alliance between the two countries.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/April%202024/USSEC%201.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-04-05T09:10:40+08:00","hits":676},{"id":531,"title":"AFP holds 24th Multi-Sector Governance Council Meeting","slug":"afp-holds-24th-multi-sector-governance-council-meeting","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Armed Forces of the Philippines’ Multi-Sector Governance Council (MSGC) held its 24th Regular Meeting on April 3 at the AFP General Headquarters here.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the AFP, and Mr Francisco Del Rosario Jr, MSGC Chairperson, presided over the meeting that was geared at pursuing transparency and accountability by seeking the civilian sector’s perspective on the AFP’s transformation initiative.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/April%202024/FOR4.jpg","image_caption":"General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, and Mr Francisco Del Rosario Jr, AFP Multi-Sector Governance Council (AFP MSGC) chairperson, pose for a photo with AFP MSGC members and senior officers of the AFP General Headquarters during the 24th AFP MSGC Regular Meeting on April 3 in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-04-04T13:30:23+08:00","hits":817},{"id":532,"title":"TDCSAFP welcomes Vietnamese Ambassador to AFP","slug":"tdcsafp-welcomes-vietnamese-ambassador-to-afp","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—LtGen Charlton Sean Gaerlan, The Deputy Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (TDCSAFP), welcomed His Excellency Lai Thai Binh, Vietnam Ambassador to the Philippines during his courtesy visit on April 4 to the AFP General Headquarters.</p>\r\n<p>In their meeting, LtGen Gaerlan thanked the Ambassador for Vietnam’s continued military cooperation with the AFP. He also reiterated the AFP's position in promoting a rules-based approach in the South China Sea.  </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/April%202024/tdcVIE%201.jpg","image_caption":"Vietnamese Ambassador Lai Thai Binh receives a token of appreciation from LtGen Charlton Sean Gaerlan, The Deputy Chief of Staff Armed Forces of the Philippines, during his visit to the AFP General Headquarters on April 4.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-04-04T13:28:40+08:00","hits":876},{"id":533,"title":"AFP senior leaders convene in GAD forum","slug":"afp-senior-leaders-convene-in-gad-forum","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—Senior leaders of the Armed Forces of the Philippines convened in a forum on April 2 here to consolidate support for gender and development programs in the military.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In partnership with United Nations Women Philippines and the Philippine Commission on Women, the Senior Leaders’ Forum on Gender and Development became an avenue for discussions on women participation in government and highlighted their role in peace and security. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/April%202024/LF4.jpg","image_caption":"LtGen Charlton Sean Gaerlan, The Deputy Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, signs the gender and development commitment board during the Senior Leaders' Forum on Gender and Development on April 2 in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-04-03T07:42:11+08:00","hits":904},{"id":534,"title":"CSAFP boards visiting Australian frigate","slug":"csafp-boards-visiting-australian-frigate","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City--General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, boarded HMAS Warramunga in a tour hosted by its commanding officer, Commander Jennifer Graham, on April 2 in Puerto Princesa City.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">HMAS WARRAMUNGA, a long-range frigate capable of air defence, surface and undersea warfare, surveillance, reconnaissance and interdiction, is in a port call in Palawan. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The call and visit is part of the AFP's military diplomacy activities aimed at strengthening military relations with partner nations. It is also covered under the PH-AUS Status of Visiting Forces Agreement.</p>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/April%202024/AWES5.jpg","image_caption":"General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, meets the officers of HMAS Warramunga during his shipboard tour on April 2 in Puerto Princesa, Palawan.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-04-03T07:40:02+08:00","hits":706},{"id":535,"title":"AFP STATEMENT | On the occasion of the New People's Army anniversary ","slug":"afp-statement-on-the-occasion-of-the-new-peoples-army-anniversary","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p>I urge every remaining member of the New People's Army (NPA) to take a moment of reflection and reconsideration. The armed struggle only brought about suffering and division. It is time to break the cycle of violence and embrace the possibility of peace. It is time to lay down your arms and abandon the armed struggle. </p>\r\n<p>The opportunity to reintegrate into society, to reunite with your loved ones, and to lead productive lives awaits you. Let us not allow ourselves to be further ensnared in the web of conflict and strife. It is time to chart a new course towards reconciliation and healing.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/March%202024/NPAANIV%201.jpg","image_caption":"Message of General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines on the occasion of the New People's Army anniversary on March 29, 2024.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-03-30T09:28:35+08:00","hits":996},{"id":536,"title":"CSAFP urges WESCOM troops to stay determined amid challenges","slug":"csafp-urges-wescom-troops-to-stay-determined-amid-challenges","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, urged soldiers of the Western Command to continue with determination in their mission amid challenges to Philippine sovereign rights in the West Philippine Sea.</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/March%202024/WIA%201.jpg","image_caption":"General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, visits and checks on the welfare of a personnel injured in the latest rotation and reprovisioning mission during his visit to the WESCOM headquarters in Palawan on March 26.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-03-27T09:23:28+08:00","hits":422},{"id":537,"title":"AFP joins national earthquake drill","slug":"afp-joins-national-earthquake-drill","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The officers, enlisted personnel, and civilian human resource of the Armed Forces of the Philippines joined on March 25 here the 1st Quarter National Simultaneous Earthquake Drill aimed at increasing public awareness and preparation for earthquakes and other natural calamities.</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/March%202024/EQ%201.jpg","image_caption":"BGen Armand Arevalo (4th from left), Commander of the General Headquarters and Headquarters Service Command, inspects the command and control tent during the 1st Quarter National Simultaneous Earthquake Drill on March 25 in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.  Photo by SSg Amagan/PAOAFP","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-03-25T09:17:26+08:00","hits":296},{"id":538,"title":"AFP Fun Run Unites Forces for Gender Equality","slug":"afp-fun-run-unites-forces-for-gender-equality","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City -- The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) Gender and Development Office (GADO) held a Fun Run today, March 23, 2024 at the Lapu-Lapu Grandstand to celebrate National Women's Month. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Quezon City Councilor and Chairperson for Committee on Women, Family Relations and Gender Equality Hon. Maria Eleanor R. Juan represented Mayor Joy Belmonte as the Guest of Honor and Speaker during the event. The Deputy Chief of Staff, AFP, LtGen Charlton Sean Gaerlan PN(M), and Colonel Arlene Frage Chief, GADO were also present.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/March%202024/FR.jpg","image_caption":"Top 3 female finishers in 5KM distance category are awarded with medals during the National Women’s Month Celebration Fun Run at the Lapu-Lapu Grandstand.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-03-23T09:44:48+08:00","hits":880},{"id":539,"title":"Unaizah May 4 returns to complete RoRe mission","slug":"unaizah-may-4-returns-to-complete-rore-mission","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—Unaizah May 4 (UM4), a civilian vessel contracted to conduct a rotation and resupply (RoRe) operation at Ayungin Shoal, embarked again on March 22 to complete its mission to sustain Philippine troops stationed at BRP Sierra Madre.</span></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">UM4 is one of two civilian vessels involved in the RoRe mission last March 5. Due to damage sustained during water cannoning by the China Coast Guard, UM4 was unable to complete its mission.","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/March%202024/UM.jpg","image_caption":"Unaizah May 4 prepares for departure from Naval Detachment Oyster Bay in Puerto Princesa City, Palawan on March 22 to embark on its rotation and reprovisioning mission at BRP Sierra Madre at Ayungin Shoal.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-03-23T09:41:08+08:00","hits":870},{"id":540,"title":"AFP welcomes new VISCOM commander","slug":"afp-welcomes-new-viscom-commander","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City--The Armed Forces of the Philippines installed a new commander of the Visayas Command on March 21 following the retirement of LtGen Benedict Arevalo who bowed out of military service after over 38 years as a military officer and cadet.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In a joint retirement and change of command ceremony presided by AFP Chief of Staff General Romeo Brawner Jr, LtGen Arevalo was replaced by his deputy, Commodore Oscar Canlas Jr, who will lead the AFP's campaigns in the Visayas in an acting capacity. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/March%202024/ccc.jpg","image_caption":"General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, turns over the unit flag from LtGen Benedict Arevalo to Commodore Oscar Canlas Jr during the Change of Command Ceremomy for the Visayas Command on March 21.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-03-21T13:30:46+08:00","hits":2757},{"id":541,"title":"CA approves promotion of 129 military officers","slug":"ca-approves-promotion-of-129-military-officers-2","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Commission on Appointments approved the ad interim promotion of 129 military officers during the plenary session and deliberation in Pasay City on March 19.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/March%202024/ca2%201.jpg","image_caption":"125 military officers pose for a photo with the Commission on Appointments following the confirmation of their ad interim appointments on March 19 in Pasay City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-03-19T13:50:00+08:00","hits":691},{"id":542,"title":"PH-JP senior enlisted leaders meet","slug":"ph-jp-senior-enlisted-leaders-meet","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The senior enlisted leaders of the Armed Forces of the Philippines and the Japan Self Defense Force sat down at a meeting with LtGen Charlton Sean Gaerlan, The Deputy Chief of Staff AFP, on March 19 at the AFP General Headquarters here.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/March%202024/PHJP3.jpg","image_caption":"LtGen Charlton Sean Gaerlan, The Deputy Chief of Staff AFP, welcomes Warrant Officer Kai Osamu, Senior Enlisted Advisor to the Chief of Staff, Joint Staff, Japan Ministry of Defense, during the latter's visit in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City on March 19.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-03-19T13:48:19+08:00","hits":406},{"id":543,"title":"CSAFP visits wake of fallen soldiers","slug":"csafp-visits-wake-of-fallen-soldiers","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, visited on March 18 the wake for soldiers killed in action at the headquarters of the 6th Infantry Division in Datu Odin Sinsuat, Maguindanao. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The CSAFP also extended his condolences to the families of the four military personnel--identified the fallen troops as Private Marvin Dumaguing, Private Jessie James Corpuz, Private First Class Carl Araña, and Corporal Creszaldy Espartero--who were ambushed by the Dawlah Islamiyah-Hassan Group in Datu Hoffer. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/March%202024/KIA.jpg","image_caption":"General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, and MGen Alex Rillera, Commander of the 6th Infantry Division, render their salute to one of the fallen soldiers during their wake on March 18 in Datu Odin Sinsuat, Maguindanao.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-03-19T13:45:48+08:00","hits":484},{"id":544,"title":"CSAFP visits Special Forces Regiment","slug":"csafp-visits-special-forces-regiment","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, who is celebrating his birthday today, March 18, visited the Special Forces Regiment based in Fort Magsaysay, Nueva Ecija.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The CSAFP, who is sharing a birthday with the late President and founder of the Special Forces in the AFP, lauded the progress of the regiment since it started as the First Special Forces Company in 1962. He also reiterated his call for a united and strong AFP.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/March%202024/SFR1.jpg","image_caption":"General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, meets the officers of the Special Forces Regiment during his visit on March 18 at their headquarters in Nueva Ecija.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-03-18T06:51:12+08:00","hits":611},{"id":545,"title":"STATEMENT | On the ambush of 4 soldiers in Maguindanao del Sur","slug":"statement-on-the-ambush-of-4-soldiers-in-maguindanao-del-sur","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p>The Armed Forces of the Philippines extends its condolences to the families and loved ones left behind by four of our brave soldiers killed in an attack perpetrated by the terrorist Dawla Islamiyah - Hassan Group in Datu Hoffer Ampatuan, Maguindanao del Sur on Sunday, March 17. </p>\r\n<p>The AFP vows to hunt down the perpetrators and neutralize these ruthless killers to finally put a stop to their violent acts that disrupt peace and stability in the region.</p>\r\n<p>We assure the Filipinos that your Armed Forces is firm on its resolve to perform our mandate of protecting the people and the state.</p>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/March%202024/STATE4SD.jpg","image_caption":"Statement on the ambush of 4 soldiers in Maguindanao del Sur","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-03-18T05:04:02+08:00","hits":944},{"id":546,"title":"TDCSAFP welcomes AFP’s celebrity reservists to GHQ","slug":"tdcsafp-welcomes-afp-s-celebrity-reservists-to-ghq","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—LtGen Charlton Sean Gaerlan, The Deputy Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, received celebrity reservists Major Jose Sixto “Dingdong” Dantes and CMO2 Kristine Ann Lim at the AFP General Headquarters during their courtesy visit on March 15. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">During their visit, the Philippine Navy and CMO2 Lim also turned over two art pieces from her Bridging Horizons project aimed at promoting diplomacy and civil-military operations through cultural and artistic exchange reserve force participation.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/March%202024/DDD2.jpg","image_caption":"LtGen Charlton Sean Gaerlan, The Deputy Chief of Staff AFP, and senior military officers pose for a photo with reservists Major Jose Sixto Dantes and CMO2 Kristine Ann Lim during their visit on March 15 in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-03-15T08:28:51+08:00","hits":1423},{"id":547,"title":"CA confirms promotion of 9 senior military officers ","slug":"ca-confirms-promotion-of-9-senior-military-officers","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The interim promotion of nine senior military officers were approved by the Commission of Appointments (CA) during the plenary session presided by Senate President and CA chairperson Juan Miguel Zubiri on March 12 in Pasay City. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/March%202024/CAC1.jpg","image_caption":"Senior officers of the AFP and other government officials awaiting confirmation of the Commission on Appointments stand up for the singing of the national anthem during the plenary session on March 12 in Pasay City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-03-13T08:19:36+08:00","hits":1280},{"id":548,"title":"AFP, USINDOPACOM assure continued cooperation","slug":"afp-usindopacom-assure-continued-cooperation","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) and the United States Indo-Pacific Command (USINDOPACOM) assured continued cooperation during the meeting between AFP Chief of Staff General Romeo Brawner Jr and USINDOPACOM commander Admiral John Aquilino on March 12 at the AFP General Headquarters here. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/March%202024/pim%201.jpg","image_caption":"General Romeo Brawner Jr PA, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, renders arrival honors to Admiral John Aquilino, Commander of the US Indo-Pacific Command, during the latter's visit to the AFP General Headquarters on March 12 in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-03-12T09:47:21+08:00","hits":930},{"id":549,"title":"CSAFP sends off President Marcos Jr ","slug":"csafp-sends-off-president-marcos-jr","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, led the send off ceremony for President Ferdinand Marcos Jr at the Villamor Air Base on March 11.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Commander in Chief will be visiting Germany and the Czech Republic from March 11 to 15 to strengthen bilateral relations and foster increased cooperation with the two nations.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/March%202024/marc%201.jpg","image_caption":"President Ferdinand Marcos Jr and General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, shake hands during the send-off ceremony for the Commander in Chief and the First Lady at the Villamor Air Base in Pasay City on March 11.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-03-11T09:43:30+08:00","hits":743},{"id":550,"title":"Statement of General Romeo S Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, on the willingness of Filipinos to fight for country.","slug":"statement-of-general-romeo-s-brawner-jr-chief-of-staff-of-the-armed-forces-of-the-philippines-on-the-willingness-of-filipinos-to-fight-for-country","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/March%202024/scw%201.jpg","image_caption":"Statement of General Romeo S Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, on the willingness of Filipinos to fight for country.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-03-11T09:26:57+08:00","hits":1133},{"id":551,"title":"READ | Statement of General Romeo S Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, on the result of the OCTA Research Fourth Quarter 2023 Tugon ng Masa Survey. ","slug":"read-statement-of-general-romeo-s-brawner-jr-chief-of-staff-of-the-armed-forces-of-the-philippines-on-the-result-of-the-octa-research-fourth-quarter-2023-tugon-ng-masa-survey","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/2024/Octa.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-03-11T07:05:24+08:00","hits":755},{"id":552,"title":"46 military officers get CA nod","slug":"46-military-officers-get-ca-nod","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City-The ad interim appointments of 46 generals, flag officers, and senior officers of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) were confirmed by the Commission on Appointments (CA) on March 6 at the plenary session presided over by Senate President and CA Chairperson Juan Miguel Zubiri. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/March%202024/CA6.jpg","image_caption":"Generals/Flag Officers and Senior Officers of the Armed Forces of the Philippines pose for a photo with the Commission on Appointments headed by Chairperson Juan Miguel Zubiri on March 6.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-03-07T02:27:54+08:00","hits":1403},{"id":553,"title":"AFP sustains its forces in BRP Sierra Madre","slug":"afp-sustains-its-forces-in-brp-sierra-madre","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City —The Armed Forces of the Philippines through its Western Command is conducting a rotation and reprovisioning of troops stationed at BRP Sierra Madre (LS57) in Ayungin Shoal today, March 5.</p>\r\n<p>The RoRe mission will involve two civilian contracted vessels (Unaizah May 1 and 4) supported by Philippine Navy and Philippine Coast Guard ships.</p>\r\n<p>This action is a routine task to sustain military forces deployed in the West Philippine Sea and maintain Philippine presence in its exclusive economic zone. It also demonstrates the AFP's commitment to ensuring that every Filipino will rightfully benefit from this resource-rich region.</p>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/277351763_332811928881224_7440173074601394112_n.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-03-05T15:41:44+08:00","hits":1079},{"id":554,"title":"RORE MISSION","slug":"rore-mission","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The rotation and reprovisioning of troops conducted by the Armed Forces of the Philippines and its Western Command for troops stationed at BRP Sierra Madre (LS57) in Ayungin Shoal today, March 5. While in the mission, the two civilian vessels (Unaizah May 1 and 4) and their Philippine Navy and Philippine Coast Guard escorts were harassed, blocked, and blasted with water cannon by Chinese coast guard vessels.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Said dangerous maneuvers at sea that put the lives of Filipino personnel at risk were properly documented, adding to a long list of incidents of  Chinese coast guard and maritime militia's illegal and irresponsible actions within our exclusive economic zone.</p>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/March%202024/P4.jpg","image_caption":"A Chinese Coast Guard vessel deploys at around 8:15 a.m. its water cannon on Unaizah May 4 (UM4) during its rotation and reprovisioning mission to BRP Sierra Madre (LS57) at Ayungin Shoal on March 5.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-03-05T09:00:04+08:00","hits":4974},{"id":555,"title":"AFP joins National Women’s Month Celebration 2024","slug":"afp-joins-national-women-s-month-celebration-2024","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Armed Forces of the Philippines joined the National Women’s Month Celebration 2024 with a simultaneous flag-raising and kick-off ceremony on March 4 at the General Headquarters here. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">A series of activities was prepared in line with this year’s theme, “Lipunang Patas sa Bagong Pilipinas: Kakayahan ng Kababaihan, Patutunayan.” An exhibit dubbed as, “HERStory of Women, Peace, and Security in the AFP” was also launched that will showcase milestones in women empowerment and gender equality programs in the military.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/March%202024/KWM1.jpg","image_caption":"LtGen Arthur Cordura, the Vice Chief of Staff AFP, and BGen Charito Plaza (Res) lead the ribbon ceremony for the photo exhibition in line with the National Women's Month Celebration on March 4 in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-03-04T07:37:11+08:00","hits":1773},{"id":556,"title":"AFP welcomes new SOLCOM commander","slug":"afp-welcomes-new-solcom-commander","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City--The Armed Forces of the Philippines welcomed MGen Facundo Palafox IV as he takes the helm of the Southern Luzon Command (SOLCOM) in a change of command ceremony on March 2 in SOLCOM's headquarters in Lucena City, Quezon.<br /></span></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">The ceremony, presided by AFP Chief of Staff General Romeo Brawner Jr, also rendered honors to the outgoing commander, LtGen Efren Baluyot, who bowed out of service after over 39 years as a military officer and cadet.","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/March%202024/429821547_777068644455548_5193741700392732294_n%201.jpg","image_caption":"General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, turns over the Command Symbol to MGen Facundo Palafox IV during the Change of Command Ceremony of the Southern Luzon Command on March 2 in Lucena City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-03-02T11:48:52+08:00","hits":3914},{"id":557,"title":"Notice of Vacancy at the Public Affairs Office AFP","slug":"notice-of-vacancy-at-the-public-affairs-office-afp","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"x1e56ztr\"><span class=\"x193iq5w xeuugli x13faqbe x1vvkbs x1xmvt09 x6prxxf xvq8zen xo1l8bm xzsf02u\"><br />The Public Affairs Office of the Armed Forces of the Philippines is looking for three qualified individuals to fill-up the following vacant permanent positions:</span></div>\r\n<div class=\"x1e56ztr\"> </div>\r\n<div class=\"x1e56ztr\"><strong><span class=\"x193iq5w xeuugli x13faqbe x1vvkbs x1xmvt09 x6prxxf xvq8zen xo1l8bm xzsf02u\">1. Administrative Officer II (Information Officer I)</span></strong></div>\r\n<div class=\"x1e56ztr\"><span class=\"x193iq5w xeuugli x13faqbe x1vvkbs x1xmvt09 x6prxxf xvq8zen xo1l8bm xzsf02u\">a. Item No: AFP-GHQC-ADOFII-149-2013</span></div>\r\n<div class=\"x1e56ztr\"><span class=\"x193iq5w xeuugli x13faqbe x1vvkbs x1xmvt09 x6prxxf xvq8zen xo1l8bm xzsf02u\">b. Education: Bachelor’s Degree</span></div>\r\n<div class=\"x1e56ztr\"><span class=\"x193iq5w xeuugli x13faqbe x1vvkbs x1xmvt09 x6prxxf xvq8zen xo1l8bm xzsf02u\">c. Training: None required</span></div>\r\n<div class=\"x1e56ztr\"><span class=\"x193iq5w xeuugli x13faqbe x1vvkbs x1xmvt09 x6prxxf xvq8zen xo1l8bm xzsf02u\">d. Experience: None required</span></div>\r\n<div class=\"x1e56ztr\"><span class=\"x193iq5w xeuugli x13faqbe x1vvkbs x1xmvt09 x6prxxf xvq8zen xo1l8bm xzsf02u\">e. Responsibilities:</span></div>\r\n<div class=\"x1e56ztr\"><span class=\"x193iq5w xeuugli x13faqbe x1vvkbs x1xmvt09 x6prxxf xvq8zen xo1l8bm xzsf02u\">-Assist in planning, developing, and crafting of public information materials, external and internal messages, and other public affairs collaterals, especially audio-visual presentations and promotional videos;</span></div>\r\n<div class=\"x1e56ztr\"><span class=\"x193iq5w xeuugli x13faqbe x1vvkbs x1xmvt09 x6prxxf xvq8zen xo1l8bm xzsf02u\">-Conceptualize, propose, and manage the creation of engaging contents for AFP social media platforms;</span></div>\r\n<div class=\"x1e56ztr\"><span class=\"x193iq5w xeuugli x13faqbe x1vvkbs x1xmvt09 x6prxxf xvq8zen xo1l8bm xzsf02u\">-Prepare storyboards, scripts, and interview points for promotional content;</span></div>\r\n<div class=\"x1e56ztr\"><span class=\"x193iq5w xeuugli x13faqbe x1vvkbs x1xmvt09 x6prxxf xvq8zen xo1l8bm xzsf02u\">-Assist in the management of AFP social media platforms;</span></div>\r\n<div class=\"x1e56ztr\"><span class=\"x193iq5w xeuugli x13faqbe x1vvkbs x1xmvt09 x6prxxf xvq8zen xo1l8bm xzsf02u\">-Assist in the execution of information and public relations activities like press conferences, in-office and studio interviews, and other media engagements.</span></div>\r\n<div class=\"x1e56ztr\"> </div>\r\n<div class=\"x1e56ztr\"><strong><span class=\"x193iq5w xeuugli x13faqbe x1vvkbs x1xmvt09 x6prxxf xvq8zen xo1l8bm xzsf02u\">2. Administrative Officer II (Information Officer I)</span></strong></div>\r\n<div class=\"x1e56ztr\"><span class=\"x193iq5w xeuugli x13faqbe x1vvkbs x1xmvt09 x6prxxf xvq8zen xo1l8bm xzsf02u\">a. Item No: AFP-GHQC-ADOFII-148-2013</span></div>\r\n<div class=\"x1e56ztr\"><span class=\"x193iq5w xeuugli x13faqbe x1vvkbs x1xmvt09 x6prxxf xvq8zen xo1l8bm xzsf02u\">b. Education: Bachelor’s Degree</span></div>\r\n<div class=\"x1e56ztr\"><span class=\"x193iq5w xeuugli x13faqbe x1vvkbs x1xmvt09 x6prxxf xvq8zen xo1l8bm xzsf02u\">c. Training: None required</span></div>\r\n<div class=\"x1e56ztr\"><span class=\"x193iq5w xeuugli x13faqbe x1vvkbs x1xmvt09 x6prxxf xvq8zen xo1l8bm xzsf02u\">d. Experience: None required</span></div>\r\n<div class=\"x1e56ztr\"><span class=\"x193iq5w xeuugli x13faqbe x1vvkbs x1xmvt09 x6prxxf xvq8zen xo1l8bm xzsf02u\">e. Responsibilities:</span></div>\r\n<div class=\"x1e56ztr\"><span class=\"x193iq5w xeuugli x13faqbe x1vvkbs x1xmvt09 x6prxxf xvq8zen xo1l8bm xzsf02u\">-Assist in planning, developing, and crafting public information materials, external and internal messaging, and other public affairs collaterals;</span></div>\r\n<div class=\"x1e56ztr\"><span class=\"x193iq5w xeuugli x13faqbe x1vvkbs x1xmvt09 x6prxxf xvq8zen xo1l8bm xzsf02u\">-Handle administrative requests, prepare communications, and organize and schedule appointments;</span></div>\r\n<div class=\"x1e56ztr\"><span class=\"x193iq5w xeuugli x13faqbe x1vvkbs x1xmvt09 x6prxxf xvq8zen xo1l8bm xzsf02u\">-Set up meetings, liaise with internal and external stakeholders, and take detailed minutes of meetings;</span></div>\r\n<div class=\"x1e56ztr\"><span class=\"x193iq5w xeuugli x13faqbe x1vvkbs x1xmvt09 x6prxxf xvq8zen xo1l8bm xzsf02u\">-Assist in the execution of information and public relations activities like press conferences, in-office and studio interviews, and other media engagements.</span></div>\r\n<div class=\"x1e56ztr\"> </div>\r\n<div class=\"x1e56ztr\"><strong><span class=\"x193iq5w xeuugli x13faqbe x1vvkbs x1xmvt09 x6prxxf xvq8zen xo1l8bm xzsf02u\">3. Administrative Assistant II</span></strong></div>\r\n<div class=\"x1e56ztr\"><span class=\"x193iq5w xeuugli x13faqbe x1vvkbs x1xmvt09 x6prxxf xvq8zen xo1l8bm xzsf02u\">a. Item No: AFP-GHQC-ADAS2-147-2013</span></div>\r\n<div class=\"x1e56ztr\"><span class=\"x193iq5w xeuugli x13faqbe x1vvkbs x1xmvt09 x6prxxf xvq8zen xo1l8bm xzsf02u\">b. Education: Completion of two years studies in College or High School</span></div>\r\n<div class=\"x1e56ztr\"><span class=\"x193iq5w xeuugli x13faqbe x1vvkbs x1xmvt09 x6prxxf xvq8zen xo1l8bm xzsf02u\">Graduate with relevant vocational/trade course</span></div>\r\n<div class=\"x1e56ztr\"><span class=\"x193iq5w xeuugli x13faqbe x1vvkbs x1xmvt09 x6prxxf xvq8zen xo1l8bm xzsf02u\">c. Training: Four (4) hours of relevant training</span></div>\r\n<div class=\"x1e56ztr\"><span class=\"x193iq5w xeuugli x13faqbe x1vvkbs x1xmvt09 x6prxxf xvq8zen xo1l8bm xzsf02u\">d. Experience: One (1) year of relevant experience</span></div>\r\n<div class=\"x1e56ztr\"><span class=\"x193iq5w xeuugli x13faqbe x1vvkbs x1xmvt09 x6prxxf xvq8zen xo1l8bm xzsf02u\">e. Responsibilities:</span></div>\r\n<div class=\"x1e56ztr\"><span class=\"x193iq5w xeuugli x13faqbe x1vvkbs x1xmvt09 x6prxxf xvq8zen xo1l8bm xzsf02u\">-Assist in the preparation and processing of cash disbursement, purchase orders, and cash advance and liquidation;</span></div>\r\n<div class=\"x1e56ztr\"><span class=\"x193iq5w xeuugli x13faqbe x1vvkbs x1xmvt09 x6prxxf xvq8zen xo1l8bm xzsf02u\">-Assist in the preparation of financial reports and records and maintenance of manual books of accounts;</span></div>\r\n<div class=\"x1e56ztr\"><span class=\"x193iq5w xeuugli x13faqbe x1vvkbs x1xmvt09 x6prxxf xvq8zen xo1l8bm xzsf02u\">-Monitor contracts and obligations and ensure timely payment of subscriptions;</span></div>\r\n<div class=\"x1e56ztr\"><span class=\"x193iq5w xeuugli x13faqbe x1vvkbs x1xmvt09 x6prxxf xvq8zen xo1l8bm xzsf02u\">-Maintain organized and up-to-date financial records, including filing and archiving of documents;</span></div>\r\n<div class=\"x1e56ztr\"><span class=\"x193iq5w xeuugli x13faqbe x1vvkbs x1xmvt09 x6prxxf xvq8zen xo1l8bm xzsf02u\">-Assist in the overall execution of Office activities like press conferences, in-office and studio interviews, and other media engagements.</span></div>\r\n<div class=\"x1e56ztr\"> </div>\r\n<div class=\"x1e56ztr\"><span class=\"x193iq5w xeuugli x13faqbe x1vvkbs x1xmvt09 x6prxxf xvq8zen xo1l8bm xzsf02u\">Interested applicants should signify their interest in writing by submitting an application letter with the following attachments not later than 15 March 2024:</span></div>\r\n<div class=\"x1e56ztr\"><span class=\"x193iq5w xeuugli x13faqbe x1vvkbs x1xmvt09 x6prxxf xvq8zen xo1l8bm xzsf02u\">1. Letter of Intent/Cover Letter</span></div>\r\n<div class=\"x1e56ztr\"><span class=\"x193iq5w xeuugli x13faqbe x1vvkbs x1xmvt09 x6prxxf xvq8zen xo1l8bm xzsf02u\">2. Fully accomplished Personal Data Sheet (PDS) with recent passport-sized picture (CS Form No. 212, Revised 2017) which can be downloaded at www.csc.gov.ph;</span></div>\r\n<div class=\"x1e56ztr\"><span class=\"x193iq5w xeuugli x13faqbe x1vvkbs x1xmvt09 x6prxxf xvq8zen xo1l8bm xzsf02u\">3. Performance rating in the present position for one (1) year (if applicable);</span></div>\r\n<div class=\"x1e56ztr\"><span class=\"x193iq5w xeuugli x13faqbe x1vvkbs x1xmvt09 x6prxxf xvq8zen xo1l8bm xzsf02u\">4. Photocopy of certificate of eligibility/rating/license; and</span></div>\r\n<div class=\"x1e56ztr\"><span class=\"x193iq5w xeuugli x13faqbe x1vvkbs x1xmvt09 x6prxxf xvq8zen xo1l8bm xzsf02u\">5. Photocopy of Transcript of Records/Diploma.</span></div>\r\n<div class=\"x1e56ztr\"> </div>\r\n<div class=\"x1e56ztr\"><span class=\"x193iq5w xeuugli x13faqbe x1vvkbs x1xmvt09 x6prxxf xvq8zen xo1l8bm xzsf02u\">Incomplete submissions will not be entertained. Regrettably, only shortlisted applicants will be contacted. Qualified applicants are advised to address and send their applications to (email applications use the prescribed subject [Application_Full Name_Item Number]):</span></div>\r\n<div class=\"x1e56ztr\"> </div>\r\n<div class=\"x1e56ztr\"><span class=\"x193iq5w xeuugli x13faqbe x1vvkbs x1xmvt09 x6prxxf xvq8zen xo1l8bm xzsf02u\">COLONEL XERXES A TRINIDAD PA(MNSA)</span></div>\r\n<div class=\"x1e56ztr\"><span class=\"x193iq5w xeuugli x13faqbe x1vvkbs x1xmvt09 x6prxxf xvq8zen xo1l8bm xzsf02u\">Chief, Public Affairs Office, AFP</span></div>\r\n<div class=\"x1e56ztr\"><span class=\"x193iq5w xeuugli x13faqbe x1vvkbs x1xmvt09 x6prxxf xvq8zen xo1l8bm xzsf02u\">Camp General Emilio Aguinaldo, Quezon City</span></div>\r\n<div class=\"x1e56ztr\"><span class=\"x193iq5w xeuugli x13faqbe x1vvkbs x1xmvt09 x6prxxf xvq8zen xo1l8bm xzsf02u\">paoafp@gmail.com</span></div>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Notice%20of%20Vacancy_Feb%202024_page-0001.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":true,"published_at":"2024-03-01T06:53:29+08:00","hits":2283},{"id":558,"title":"AFP among Metrobank Foundation's PEACE awardees","slug":"afp-among-metrobank-foundations-peace-awardees","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City--The Armed Forces of the Philippines was bestowed the 4th Metrobank Foundation Award for Partner in Empowerment, Advocacy, and Commitment to Excellence (PEACE) during the 45th founding anniversary of Metrobank Foundation Inc., (MBFI) on February 29 in Taguig City.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/March%202024/nr2.jpg","image_caption":"AFP Chief of Staff General Romeo Brawner (middle, front row) poses for a photo with other recipients of the Partners in Empowerment, Advocacy, and Commitment to Excellence (PEACE) award during the 45 foundaing anniversary of Metrobank Foundation Inc., (MBFI) on February 29 in Taguig City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-03-01T01:41:34+08:00","hits":843},{"id":559,"title":"Troops neutralize high ranking NPA leader in Zamboanga del Sur","slug":"troops-neutralize-high-ranking-npa-leader-in-zamboanga-del-sur","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The 102nd Infantry Brigade of the Philippine Army  neutralized the Secretary of the Western Mindanao Regional Party Committee (WMRPC) of the Communist Party of the Philippines-New People's Army-National Democratic Front (CPP-NPA-NDF) during an encounter in Brgy. Malagalad, Dumingag, Zamboanga Del Sur on February 27. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Aprecia Rosete @ Bambam, the Secretary of WMRPC, died in a clash with Army troops. She is known to be the mastermind behind heinous acts in Zamboanga Peninsula such as extortion, murder of innocent civilians, and destructive sabotage of critical infrastructure projects with over 30 warrants of arrest against her.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/February%202024/viber_image_2024-02-27_19-28-28-853%201.jpg","image_caption":"An NPA leader died in a clash with Army troops in Brgy. Malagalad, Dumingag, Zamboanga Del Sur on February 27, 2024.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-02-27T08:41:56+08:00","hits":1400},{"id":560,"title":"AFP, Okada Foundation ink agreement on Dental Equipment Donation","slug":"afp-okada-foundation-ink-agreement-on-dental-equipment-donation","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Chief of Staff, Armed Forces of the Philippines, General Romeo S Brawner Jr. signed a Memorandum of Agreement with the Okada Foundation Inc., donating dental equipment to the AFP Dental Service, in a ceremony conducted on February 26 at the General Headquarters. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/February%202024/wsas.jpg","image_caption":"The Chief of Staff, AFP, Gen. Romeo S Brawner Jr., and Okada Foundation President, Mr. James Lorenzana pose for a photo during the Ceremonial Memorandum of Agreement Signing between the AFP and Okada Foundation, Inc. on February 26, 2024 in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-02-26T14:03:50+08:00","hits":680},{"id":561,"title":"AFP strikes blow to NPA and Local Terrorist Groups in continuing nationwide sweep","slug":"afp-strikes-blow-to-npa-and-local-terrorist-groups-in-continuing-nationwide-sweep","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City -- A series of coordinated military operations have successfully targeted and eliminated key leaders and members of Communist and Local Terrorists Groups across the country in the past days.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">As of  February 15, the AFP neutralized 223 Communist Terrorist Group (CTG) members and 18 Local Terrorist Group (LTG) members. Hundreds of low-powered and high-powered firearms, including IEDs, were either seized or surrendered in the said period. Adding to these totals are recent gains as a result of focused military operations in various regions.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/February%202024/CTG.jpg","image_caption":"The leader of the remnants of the CPP-NPA Communist Terrorist Group (CTG) in Bohol along with four members, were neutralized in an encounter with the combined forces of the 47th Infantry Battalion, 302nd Brigade of the 3rd Infantry (Spearhead) Division and the combined elements of the Bohol Police Provincial Office in Purok Matin-ao 2, Barangay Campagao, Bilar, Bohol on Friday, February 23, 2024. (Photo by 3ID)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-02-25T14:01:54+08:00","hits":1855},{"id":562,"title":"US CAPSTONE Pacific Fellows visit AFP General Headquarters","slug":"us-capstone-pacific-fellows-visit-afp-general-headquarters","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"    <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines (CSAFP), welcomed the US CAPSTONE Pacific program fellows and staff during their courtesy visit to the AFP General Headquarters here on February 23.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The United States generals and flag officers were led by General John Kelly (Ret), a former White House Chief of Staff, Secretary of the Department of Homeland Security, and commander of the US Southern Command.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/February%202024/CAP2.jpg","image_caption":"General Romeo Brawner Jr, the Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, poses for a photo with the delegates and staff of the US CAPSTONE Pacific program led by retired US General John Kelly during their visit at the AFP General Headquarters on February 23.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-02-23T08:02:23+08:00","hits":764},{"id":563,"title":"AFP holds Oral Health Fair 2024","slug":"afp-holds-oral-health-fair-2024","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City — In celebration of the 20th National Oral Health Month, the Armed Forces of the Philippines Dental Service conducted the Oral Health Fair 2024 on February 21 at the Lapu-Lapu Grandstand. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In his message, the Chief of Staff, AFP, General Romeo S Brawner Jr PA, commended the AFP Dental Service personnel for their dedication towards attaining an \"Effective Preventive Dentistry Program for Sustainable Quality Oral Health for the AFP.\"</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/February%202024/DF1.jpg","image_caption":"The Deputy Chief of Staff, Armed Forces of the Philippines, LtGen Charlton Sean Gaerlan PN(M) poses for a photo with AFP Officers during the Oral Health Fair 2024 on February 21, 2024 in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-02-23T07:50:45+08:00","hits":856},{"id":564,"title":"Soldiers told to stay united, strong in CSAFP visit to Mindanao","slug":"soldiers-told-to-stay-united-strong-in-csafp-visit-to-mindanao","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"    <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines again told soldiers to stay united and strong for the country when he visited military units in Mindanao.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/February%202024/MINS.jpg","image_caption":"General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff AFP, talks to the troops of 103rd Infantry Brigade in Marawi City on February 21.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-02-23T07:49:10+08:00","hits":716},{"id":565,"title":"CSAFP lauds Visayas troops","slug":"csafp-lauds-visayas-troops","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"    <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—In continuation of his visits to military units nationwide, General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, touched down in Visayas where he lauded the accomplishments of the Visayas Command in Cebu and the 301st Infantry Brigade in Iloilo.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/February%202024/vis%201.jpg","image_caption":"General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff AFP, poses for a photo with the troops of 301st Infantry Brigade during his visit to their headquarters in Iloilo on February 22.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-02-22T08:34:16+08:00","hits":615},{"id":566,"title":"CSAFP honors troops in Marawi City","slug":"csafp-honors-troops-in-marawi-city","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, awarded medals to officers and enlisted personnel during his visit to the 103rd Infantry Brigade in Marawi City on February 21.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The soldiers, who received Gold and Silver Cross medals, were cited for their role in neutralizing members of the Dawlah Islamiyah-Maute Group responsible in the bombing at the Mindanao State University last December. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/February%202024/MAR1%201.jpg","image_caption":"General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff AFP, awards the Silver Cross Medal to Col Billy Dela Rosa during his visit to the 103rd Infantry Brigade in Marawi City on February 21.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-02-21T08:52:02+08:00","hits":788},{"id":567,"title":"CSAFP condoles with families of slain soldiers","slug":"csafp-condoles-with-families-of-slain-soldiers","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines visited and extended his condolences to the families of the six soldiers who were killed in action in Munai, Lanao Del Sur last February 18.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The CSAFP arrived at the headquarters of the 1st Infantry Division in Zamboanga Del Sur on February 20 where a vigil for the soldiers was being held. There he assured the families of the AFP’s full support and assistance.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/February%202024/viber_image_2024-02-20_20-42-19-995%201.jpg","image_caption":"General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, pays his respects to one of the slain soldiers during a vigil at the 1st Infantry Division headquarters in Zamboanga Del Sur on February 20.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-02-20T08:56:42+08:00","hits":846},{"id":568,"title":"AFP, BFFI, World of Outbound Corp seal partnership","slug":"afp-bffi-world-of-outbound-corp-seal-partnership","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"    <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP), through the Office of the Deputy Chief of Staff for Civil-Military Operations (CMO), J7, conducted a Partnership Agreement Signing with the Bayan Family of Foundations, Inc. (BFFI) and World of Outbound Corporation on February 20 at the General Headquarters. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/February%202024/viber_image_2024-02-20_18-18-52-925%201.jpg","image_caption":"AFP Officers pose for a photo with Bayan Family of Foundations, Inc., and World of Outbound Corp. representatives during a Partnership Agreement Signing on February 20, 2024, in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-02-20T08:55:07+08:00","hits":1035},{"id":569,"title":"On AFP’s efforts against the terrorist Dawlah Islamiyah-Maute Group in Munai, Lanao Del Norte","slug":"on-afp-s-efforts-against-the-terrorist-dawlah-islamiyah-maute-group-in-munai-lanao-del-norte","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"    <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Armed Forces of the Philippines remains relentless in its pursuit operations against members of the Dawlah Islamiyah-Maute Group that perpetrated the bombing at Mindanao State University last year. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/February%202024/s.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-02-19T10:47:15+08:00","hits":1815},{"id":570,"title":"PH-US aircraft hold combined air patrol","slug":"ph-us-aircraft-hold-combined-air-patrol","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City--Air assets of the Philippine Air Force and the United States Pacific Air Force (PACAF) held a combined air patrol over the West Philippine Sea on February 19.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Three PAF FA-50s accompanied one B-52H bomber aircraft of PACAF in the activity that started west of Ilocos Sur and ended over Mindoro Strait. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/February%202024/mca3%201.jpg","image_caption":"A FA-50 of the Philippine Air Force during pre-flight checks ahead of the Maritime Cooperative Activity with the United States Pacific Air Force on February 19 over the West Philippine Sea.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-02-19T08:52:46+08:00","hits":757},{"id":571,"title":"AFP Excels in NATO Exercise Defense Cyber Marvel 3 with Impressive Rankings","slug":"afp-excels-in-nato-exercise-defense-cyber-marvel-3-with-impressive-rankings","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) secured high rankings in virtual challenges during the Exercise Defense Cyber Marvel 3 (DCM3) held on February 10 to 16 at Marco Polo Hotel in Pasig City. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The AFP Cyber teams ranked 3rd, 4th, and 5th places out of 127 participating teams from other countries in the Capture The Flag (CTF) Challenge, and clinched the 3rd place in the Artificial Intelligence Challenge during DCM3 led by the United Kingdom (UK) Army.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/February%202024/NAT.jpg","image_caption":"The Exercise Defense Cyber Marvel 3 held at Marco Polo Hotel, Pasig City on February 10 to 16 served as an opportunity for AFP and UK Army members to collaborate and share skills and knowledges in the field of cyber defense. (Photo from CEISSAFP)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-02-17T10:44:18+08:00","hits":1635},{"id":572,"title":"U.S. aircraft deliver more relief packs to Mindanao","slug":"u-s-aircraft-deliver-more-relief-packs-to-mindanao","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"    <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The United States Marine Corps, in collaboration with the Armed Forces of the Philippines and other government agencies, delivered more Family Food Packs to the landslide-affected areas in Davao de Oro.  </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">As of February 15, a total of 15,400 Family Food Packs from the Department of Social Welfare and Development were transported using two (2) USMC KC-130J Hercules aircraft, which ensured the prompt delivery of aid to communities in need.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/February%202024/HADR2.jpg","image_caption":"US Military and AFP troops load Family Food Packs (FFPs) for the landslide-affected communities in Davao de Oro. (Photo by Tactical Operations Wing Eastern Mindanao, PAF)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-02-15T10:10:46+08:00","hits":1068},{"id":573,"title":"AFP commits troops, assets for HADR in Mindanao","slug":"afp-commits-troops-assets-for-hadr-in-mindanao","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City — The Armed Forces of the Philippines, deployed its search and rescue personnel and assets for the ongoing humanitarian assistance and disaster response (HADR) operations in Davao and Caraga regions to assist residents affected by recent heavy rains and flooding that persist since late January and the Masara landslide on February 6.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Philippine Air Force--particularly the 505th Search and Rescue Group, 205th Tactical Helicopter Wing, and the 220th Airlift Wing--with six helicopters, one C-130, and one C-295 aircraft in use have transported a total of 88,444 lbs of relief goods, equipment, and personnel as of February 13. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/February%202024/had.jpg","image_caption":"Troops from the 25IB deliver relief supplies by foot to the isolated community of Sitio Cagan in Davao de Oro. (Photo by 25IB, Philippine Army)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-02-14T08:33:04+08:00","hits":1168},{"id":574,"title":"U.S. air assets to assist AFP in aiding Mindanao landslide victims","slug":"u-s-air-assets-to-assist-afp-in-aiding-mindanao-landslide-victims-2","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City —  In a collaborative effort between the United States Armed Forces and the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP), two (2) U.S. Marine Corps KC-130J Hercules aircraft will be providing assistance in delivering supplies to the affected communities of the Masara Landslide in Mindanao. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Currently, the two USMC KC-130 aircraft are stationed at Villamor Air Base while the processing, weighing and loading  of supplies for transport on February 12 are ongoing, with the plan for four (4) deliveries daily (two per plane) to maintain a steady supply to the affected areas. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/February%202024/PAC.jpg","image_caption":"Troops prepare for the loading of relief packs on the U.S. Marine Corps KC-130J Hercules aircraft for the affected communities of the Masara Landslide in Mindanao.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-02-12T10:26:12+08:00","hits":910},{"id":575,"title":"Two US aircraft deliver aid to Davao City","slug":"two-us-aircraft-deliver-aid-to-davao-city","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City--Two C-130 aircraft of the United States Marine Corps delivered to Davao City 4,800 boxes of family food packs of the Department of Social Welfare and Development on February 12.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/February%202024/aid.jpg","image_caption":"Personnel of the Eastern Mindanao Command Philippine Air Force and the US Marine Corps load the family food packs onto a transport truck after they were unloaded from a US C-130 aircraft at the Davao International Airport on February 12.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-02-12T09:17:47+08:00","hits":1354},{"id":576,"title":"AFP dons rank to 21 newly-promoted TAS Senior Officers","slug":"afp-dons-rank-to-21-newly-promoted-tas-senior-officers","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Deputy Chief of Staff, Armed Forces of the Philippines (TDCSAFP), LtGen Charlton Sean M Gaerlan PN(M) led the donning of ranks of 21 newly-promoted senior officers from the Technical and Administrative Services (TAS) on February 12 at the General Headquarters. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In his message, the TDCSAFP thanked the TAS officers from the AFP Medical Corps, Dental Service, Judge Advocate General's Service, Corps of Professors, and Medical Administrative Corps for their dedication and commitment to public service while upholding the values of honor, service and patriotism.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/February%202024/don.jpg","image_caption":"The Newly Promoted Technical and Administrative Services (TAS) Senior Officers pose for a photo with The Deputy Chief of Staff, AFP, LtGen Charlton Sean Gaerlan PN(M) during the Donning of Ranks of the Newly Promoted TAS Senior Officers on February 12 in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-02-12T09:14:03+08:00","hits":1227},{"id":577,"title":"PBBM visits, fetes soldiers at Army Hospital","slug":"pbbm-visits-fetes-soldiers-at-army-hospital","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City--President Ferdinand Marcos Jr along with top defense and military officials visited soldiers receiving treatment at the Army General Hospital in Fort Bonifacio on February 12.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">He also met and awarded the personnel who were wounded in the successful military operation against members of the Dawlah Islamiyah-Maute Group last January that resulted in the death of top wanted personalities in the Mindanao State University bombing last December.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/February%202024/BM4.jpg","image_caption":"President Ferdinand Marcos Jr talks to a soldier recovering at the Army General Hospital during his visit on February 12.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-02-12T09:12:23+08:00","hits":837},{"id":578,"title":"DI Amir among casualties in January ops","slug":"di-amir-among-casualties-in-january-ops","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"    <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City--The Armed Forces of the Philippines through its 103rd Infantry Brigade, Philippine Army confirmed the death of  Khadafi Mimbesa, also known as “Engineer,\" in the military operation in January in Lanao del Sur.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The efforts of the 103rd Brigade, under the leadership of their Commander, BGen Yegor Rey Barroquillo Jr, resulted in the neutralization of local terrorists and armed members of the Dawlah Islamiyah in Lanao del Sur on January 25-26, 2024, who were identified as perpetrators of the fatal bombing at Mindanao State University (MSU) on December 3, 2023.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/February%202024/TAB2.webp","image_caption":"Troops inspect the war material recovered at the site of the encounter against the Dawlah Islamiyah-Maute Group on January 25 to 26 in Lanao del Sur.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-02-12T09:01:40+08:00","hits":921},{"id":579,"title":"AFP, USINDOPACOM holds 3rd Maritime Cooperative Activity, affirm commitment to free and open Indo-Pacific","slug":"afp-usindopacom-holds-3rd-maritime-cooperative-activity-affirm-commitment-to-free-and-open-indo-pacific","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) and the United States Indo-Pacific Command (USINDOPACOM) successfully conducted the third PH-US Maritime Cooperative Activity (MCA) in the West Philippine Sea on Friday, February 9, reaffirming the countries’ commitment to bolstering regional security and stability. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Philippine Navy’s BRP Gregorio Del Pilar (PS-15) and AW109 Helicopter (NH434) together with the U.S. Navy’s USS Gabrielle Giffords (LCS 10), embarked with an MH-60S Sea Hawk, sailed together and participated in advanced planning and maritime communication operations within the Philippines’ Exclusive Economic Zone. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/February%202024/MCA3.jpg","image_caption":"Philippine Navy officers aboard BRP Gregorio Del Pilar (PS15) render passing honors to the USS Gabrielle Giffords (LCS 10) during the 3rd AFP-USINDOPACOM Maritime Cooperative Activity in the West Philippine Sea on Friday, February 9. (Photo by Western Command)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-02-09T10:13:11+08:00","hits":1057},{"id":580,"title":"TDCSAFP meets with the AFP Women’s Volleyball Team","slug":"tdcsafp-meets-with-the-afp-women-s-volleyball-team","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Deputy Chief of Staff, Armed Forces of the Philippines (TDCSAFP), LtGen Charlton Sean Gaerlan PN(M), welcomed the members of the AFP Women’s Volleyball Team during a Courtesy Call on February 07 at the General Headquarters.</span></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">During their meeting, the TDCSAFP thanked the team for their contributions to the AFP and recognized their efforts and achievements as soldier-athletes.<br /><br /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">One of the team's recent accomplishments includes being hailed as champion during the UNTV Women’s Volleyball League where they donated PhP500,000.00 to the AFP Educational Benefit System Office to support the education of soldiers’ orphans.<br /><br /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">The AFP remains committed to extending support to the AFP Women’s Volleyball Team and its soldier-athletes as they thrive and continue to represent the organization in their athletic pursuits.///<br /><br /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">(Photo by A1C Castro/PAOAFP)</div>\r\n</div>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/February%202024/VOL3.jpg","image_caption":"The Deputy Chief of Staff, AFP, LtGen Charlton Sean Gaerlan PN(M), and The Deputy Chief of Staff for Personnel, J1, MGen Rommel Roldan PAF pose for a photo with the AFP Women’s Volleyball Team during their Courtesy Call on February 07, 2024 in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-02-08T01:35:13+08:00","hits":792},{"id":581,"title":"CSAFP visits troops in northernmost military outpost","slug":"csafp-visits-troops-in-northernmost-military-outpost","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, checked on the morale and welfare of the troops stationed at Mavulis Island in Batanes on February 6.</span></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">He joined Secretary of National Defense Gilbert Teodoro Jr along with senior military and defense officials in assessing territorial defense capabilities and fortifications in the area.","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/February%202024/MAV7.jpg","image_caption":"Defense Secretary Gilbert Teodoro Jr poses for a photo with General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the AFP; Philippine Navy Flag Officer in Command VAdm Toribio Adaci Jr; Commander of Northern Luzon Command LtGen Fernyl Buca; Commodore Francisco Tagamolila, commander of Naval Forces Northern Luzon; and BGen Vicente Mark Anthony Blanco III, commander of 4th Marine Brigade; and other officials during their visit to the Naval Detachment Mavulis, Mavulis Island, Batanes on February 6.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-02-07T09:17:08+08:00","hits":1018},{"id":582,"title":"CSAFP honors SOLCOM Commander, introduces AFP’s new battle cry","slug":"csafp-honors-solcom-commander-introduces-afp-s-new-battle-cry","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City –The Chief of Staff, Armed Forces of the Philippines (CSAFP), General Romeo S Brawner Jr., led the Flag Raising Ceremony and welcomed the Commander of the Southern Luzon Command, AFP, LtGen Efren Baluyot PA, during an Exit Call conducted on February 05 at the General Headquarters.</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/February%202024/BC3.jpg","image_caption":"The Deputy Chief of Staff for Education, Training and Doctrine, J8, MGen Noel Beleran PN(M) welcomes the Commander, Southern Luzon Command, LtGen Efren Baluyot PA, during his Exit Call on February 05, 2024 in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-02-05T09:20:01+08:00","hits":1386},{"id":583,"title":"CSAFP honors soldiers of 101st Brigade","slug":"csafp-honors-soldiers-of-101st-brigade","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, General Romeo Brawner Jr, recognized soldiers for their heroism, service, and contributions to the peace and security situation in Basilan, Sulu, and nearby provinces on February 4.</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/February%202024/awa.jpg","image_caption":"General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, pins the Gawad sa Kapayapaan Award to LtCol Michael Colanta during his visit to the 101st Infantry Brigade on February 4 in Isabela City, Basilan.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-02-04T10:20:59+08:00","hits":1896},{"id":584,"title":"“Strong AFP means strong nation,” says Brawner in Mindanao visit","slug":"strong-afp-means-strong-nation-says-brawner-in-mindanao-visit","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"    <div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—General Romeo Brawner, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, emphasized that the strength of the nation depends on the strength and unity of its armed forces as he continued his visit of military camps in Mindanao, arriving at the Western Mindanao Command (WESMINCOM) headquarters in Zamboanga City and the 101st Infantry Brigade (IBde) in Isabela City, Basilan on February 4.</span></span>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/February%202024/101st.jpg","image_caption":"General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, poses for a photo with the troops of the 101st Brigade during his visit on February 4 at their headquarters in Isabela City, Basilan.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-02-04T10:18:36+08:00","hits":1852},{"id":585,"title":"CSAFP lauds troops’ HADR efforts in Southeastern Mindanao","slug":"csafp-lauds-troops-hadr-efforts-in-southeastern-mindanao","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, lauded the personnel of the 10th Infantry Division (10ID) conducting humanitarian assistance and disaster response operations in Southeastern Mindanao affected by the recent flooding.</span></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">The 10ID HADR units and personnel including 10ID's four infantry brigades, the Emergency Response Company, the Installation and Management Battalion, and the Service Support Battalion have been assisting in the evacuation efforts, clearing operations, and rescue of stranded individuals.<br /><br /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">“Nakita ko ang ginagawa ninyo para matulungan ang ating mga kababayan and I congratulate and thank all of you for doing all that and for showing the heart of the Filipino soldier in the face of these calamities,” General Brawner Jr said.</div>\r\n</div>","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/February%202024/hadr.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-02-03T10:16:16+08:00","hits":1446},{"id":586,"title":"Soldiers told to stay united in CSAFP’s visit in Davao De Oro, Davao City","slug":"soldiers-told-to-stay-united-in-csafp-s-visit-in-davao-de-oro-davao-city","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, told soldiers of the 10th Infantry Division and the Eastern Mindanao Command on February 3 to stay united and be wary of enemy efforts to infiltrate various sectors of society and challenge the AFP and the nation’s unity.</span></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">In his message to the troops in Mawab, Davao De Oro and Panacan, Davao City, he said that he is confident in the loyalty and professionalism of every member of the AFP amid recent political developments.","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/February%202024/10id.jpg","image_caption":"General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff AFP, poses for a photo with the officers and enlisted personnel of the 10th Infantry Division, on February 3 in Camp General Manuel Yan Sr, Davao de Oro.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-02-03T10:14:55+08:00","hits":1581},{"id":587,"title":"AFP joins celebration of World Hijab Day 2024","slug":"afp-joins-celebration-of-world-hijab-day-2024","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP), through the Peace and Development Office, participated in the celebration of World Hijab Day 2024 with Senator Robinhood Padilla as the Guest of Honor and Speaker on February 01 at the Lapulapu Grandstand.<br /></span></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">With the theme, “Embracing Diversity: Cultivating Peace and Development through Inclusivity,” the Chief of Staff, AFP, General Romeo S Brawner Jr., expressed his support for the celebration.","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/February%202024/hij.jpg","image_caption":"Senator Robinhood Padilla with AFP Generals, Officers and other dignitaries pose for a photo with the Hijabi troopers from the country's uniformed services during the celebration of World Hijab Day 2024 on February 01, 2024 in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-02-01T22:10:43+08:00","hits":1571},{"id":588,"title":"AFP Adjutant General’s Service celebrates 88 Years of Service","slug":"afp-adjutant-general-s-service-celebrates-88-years-of-service","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Vice Chief of Staff, Armed Forces of the Philippines (VCSAFP), LtGen Arthur Cordura PAF, joined the Office of The Adjutant General, AFP, in the celebration of the 88th Adjutant General’s Service (AGS) Anniversary on February 01 at the General Headquarters.<br /></span></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">Officers, Enlisted Personnel, and Civilian Human Resources, as well as stakeholders, were given recognition during the celebration, which focused on the theme, “88 Years of Service Excellence: Navigating Time with Unwavering Quality.”","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/January%202024/tag.jpg","image_caption":"Awardees and stakeholders pose for a photo during the 88th Adjutant General’s Service (AGS) Anniversary Celebration on February 01, 2024 in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-02-01T10:04:27+08:00","hits":2006},{"id":589,"title":"AFP concludes 2023 with resounding victories, sets goals for 2024","slug":"afp-concludes-2023-with-resounding-victories-sets-goals-for-2024","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – As 2023 ends, the Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) looks back on a year marked by notable achievements, reaffirming its commitment to national security and regional peace. These accomplishments pave the way for a dynamic and capable AFP in 2024.</span></div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">The AFP has achieved a significant milestone by dismantling eight and weakening 14 guerilla fronts of the Communist Terrorist Group (CTG). As of December, there are no more active CTG guerilla fronts. The continued focused military operations have resulted in the neutralization of 67 high-value individuals who belong to communist and local terrorist groups. Among the top leaders neutralized are Dionisio Macabalo, also known as @Muling/Kardo, who was the Secretary of the North Central Mindanao Regional Committee, and Farahudin Pumbaya Pangalian, also known as @Abu Zacharia, who was the Amir of DI-Philippines and overall Amir Islamic State-East Asia.","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/277351763_332811928881224_7440173074601394112_n.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-01-31T14:24:07+08:00","hits":3148},{"id":590,"title":"AFP hosts Year-End 2023 National JPSCC Meeting","slug":"afp-hosts-year-end-2023-national-jpscc-meeting","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) spearheaded the Year-End 2023 National Joint Peace and Security Coordinating Center (JPSCC) Meeting with the Philippine National Police (PNP) and Philippine Coast Guard (PCG) on January 30 at the General Headquarters.</span></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">The National JPSCC Meeting aims to discuss the significant accomplishments and planned activities of the six JPSCC Joint Cells: Joint Operations Cell, Joint Intelligence Cell, Joint Logistics Cell, Joint Civic-Community Relations Cell, Joint Legal and Investigation Cell, and Joint Education and Training Cell.</div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\"> </div>\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/January%202024/423248155_757744359721310_8375059160964798167_n.jpg","image_caption":"(L-R) The Deputy Chief PNP for Operations, PLtGen Michael John Dubria; The Vice Chief of Staff, AFP, LtGen Arthur Cordura PAF; The Deputy Chief of Staff, AFP, LtGen Charlton Sean Gaerlan PN(M); and Officer-in-Charge, Philippine Coast Guard, VAdm Rolando Lizor Punzalan Jr. during the Year-End 2023 National Joint Peace and Security Coordinating Center (JPSCC) Meeting on January 30, 2024 in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-01-30T10:00:51+08:00","hits":3436},{"id":591,"title":"On the AFP's Commitment to National Transformation","slug":"on-the-afps-commitment-to-national-transformation","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Armed Forces of the Philippines congratulates our Commander-in-Chief for a successful launch of the Bagong Pilipinas national effort. In heeding his call for national transformation, the AFP shall be at the vanguard. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/January%202024/STPIBP.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-01-29T09:00:20+08:00","hits":2460},{"id":592,"title":"AFP joins Send-Off Ceremony for President Marcos’ Vietnam State Visit","slug":"afp-joins-send-off-ceremony-for-president-marcos-vietnam-state-visit","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Vice Chief of Staff, Armed Forces of the Philippines, LtGen Arthur Cordura PAF, joined the Send-Off Ceremony for President Ferdinand R Marcos Jr as he embarks on a two-day State Visit to the Socialist Republic of Vietnam on January 29, 2024, at Colonel Jesus Villamor Air Base, Pasay City. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Also present during the ceremony were Philippine Air Force Commander, LtGen Stephen Parreño; Philippine Navy Flag-Officer-in-Command, VAdm Toribio Adaci Jr.; Philippine Army Vice Commander, MGen Leodevic Guinid Jr.; and Philippine National Police Chief, General Benjamin Acorda Jr.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/January%202024/SO4.jpg","image_caption":"The Vice Chief of Staff, Armed Forces of the Philippines, LtGen Arthur Cordura PAF renders Military Honors for President Ferdinand R Marcos Jr as he heads to his State Visit to the Socialist Republic of Vietnam on January 29, 2024, at Colonel Jesus Villamor Air Base, Pasay City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-01-29T08:58:13+08:00","hits":1705},{"id":593,"title":"On the neutralization of 9 Dawlah Islamiyah- Lanao involved in MSU-Marawi bombing","slug":"on-the-neutralization-of-9-dawlah-islamiyah-lanao-involved-in-msu-marawi-bombing","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Armed Forces of the Philippines commends the exceptional dedication of the 103rd Brigade, 1st Infantry Division, Philippine Army, for their successful counterterrorism operation in Barangay Tapurog, Piagapo, Lanao del Sur, on January 25 and 26, 2024. This operation resulted in the neutralization of 9 members of the Dawlah Islamiyah-Lanao and the capture of 9 high-powered firearms and two (2) Improvised Explosive Device (IED).</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/January%202024/DI-NEU.jpg","image_caption":"","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-01-27T08:54:52+08:00","hits":1999},{"id":594,"title":"AFP holds Chief of Staff Challenge 2024","slug":"afp-holds-chief-of-staff-challenge-2024","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Armed Forces of the Philippines is conducting the Chief of Staff Challenge 2024, a shooting competition sanctioned by the Philippine Shooters and Match Officers Confederation, on January 24 to 28 at the Philippine Military Academy Firing Range in Fort Del Pilar, Baguio City.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/January%202024/SC3.jpg","image_caption":"General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, during the Opening Ceremony of the Chief of Staff Challenge on January 24 in Fort Del Pilar, Baguio City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-01-24T10:09:38+08:00","hits":3445},{"id":595,"title":"AFP meets with German Director for Security and Defence Policy","slug":"afp-meets-with-german-director-for-security-and-defence-policy","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"    <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Deputy Chief of Staff, Armed Forces of the Philippines, LtGen Charlton Sean Gaerlan PN(M), met with the Director for Security and Defence Policy of the German Federal Ministry of Defence, BGen Jürgen Schrödl during a Courtesy Call on January 24 at the General Headquarters.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/January%202024/GER3.jpg","image_caption":"The Deputy Chief of Staff, Armed Forces of the Philippines, LtGen Charlton Sean Gaerlan PN(M), and the Director for Security and Defence Policy of the German Federal Ministry of Defence, BGen Jürgen Schrödl discuss PH-Germany relationship during a courtesy call on January 24, 2024 in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-01-24T10:07:57+08:00","hits":1795},{"id":596,"title":"CSAFP visits the Philippine Marine Corps","slug":"csafp-visits-the-philippine-marine-corps","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Chief of Staff, Armed Forces of the Philippines (CSAFP), General Romeo S Brawner Jr. visited the Philippine Marine Corps (PMC) on January 23 at the Headquarters, Philippine Marines, Fort Bonifacio, Taguig City. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/January%202024/mar.jpg","image_caption":"The Commandant, Philippine Marine Corps, MGen Arturo Rojas, welcomes the Chief of Staff, Armed Forces of the Philippines, Gen. Romeo S Brawner Jr, during his official visit to the Philippine Marine Corps on January 23, 2024, in Fort Bonifacio, Taguig City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-01-23T08:48:01+08:00","hits":1701},{"id":597,"title":"AFP joins commemoration of 125th Anniversary of the First Republic of the Philippines","slug":"afp-joins-commemoration-of-125th-anniversary-of-the-first-republic-of-the-philippines","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Chief of Staff, Armed Forces of the Philippines, General Romeo S Brawner Jr, joined the Commander-in-Chief, President Ferdinand R Marcos Jr, as he led the commemoration of the 125th Anniversary of the First Republic of the Philippines in a ceremony conducted on January 23 at the Barasoain Church Historical Landmark, Malolos, Bulacan.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/January%202024/Rep2.jpg","image_caption":"The Chief of Staff, Armed Forces of the Philippines, General Romeo S Brawner Jr, joins the Commander-in-Chief, President Ferdinand R Marcos Jr, as he leads the commemoration of the 125th Anniversary of the First Republic of the Philippines in a ceremony conducted on January 23 at the Barasoain Church Historical Landmark, Malolos, Bulacan.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-01-23T08:45:51+08:00","hits":1587},{"id":598,"title":"AFP inks agreement for the Philippine ROTC Games 2024","slug":"afp-inks-agreement-for-the-philippine-rotc-games-2024","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Chief of Staff, Armed Forces of the Philippines, General Romeo S Brawner Jr, joined the Ceremonial Memorandum of Agreement Signing for the Philippine Reserve Officers’ Training Corps (ROTC) Games (PRG) 2024 with PRG Honorary Chairperson, Senator Francis Tolentino, on January 22 here at the General Headquarters.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/January%202024/ROTC.jpg","image_caption":"The Chief of Staff, Armed Forces of the Philippines, Gen. Romeo S Brawner Jr; PRG Honorary Chairperson, Senator Francis Tolentino; Defense Secretary Gilberto Teodoro Jr; CHED Chairperson, Dr. J. Prospero De Vera III; and Executive Director, PSC, Mr. Paulo Francisco Tatad; and Asst. Secretary for Communication & External Affairs, DILG,  Rolando C Puno pose for a photo during the Ceremonial Memorandum of Agreement Signing for the Philippine ROTC Games 2024 on January 22, 2024, in Camp Aguinaldo.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-01-22T09:14:26+08:00","hits":2774},{"id":599,"title":"CSAFP dons higher ranks to five senior officers","slug":"csafp-dons-higher-ranks-to-five-senior-officers","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, led the donning of ranks ceremony for five recently promoted senior military officers on January 22 here.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/January%202024/OFF1.jpg","image_caption":"General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff AFP, poses for a photo with the newly promoted officers during the donning of ranks ceremony on January 22 in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-01-22T09:09:13+08:00","hits":2280},{"id":600,"title":"AFP honors soldiers' service to the nation during 88th Anniversary Celebration","slug":"afp-honors-soldiers-service-to-the-nation-during-88th-anniversary-celebration","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Armed Forces of the Philippines (AFP) celebrated its 88th Anniversary in a culminating program with the President of the Republic of the Philippines and the AFP Commander-in-Chief, His Excellency Ferdinand R Marcos Jr as the Guest of Honor and Speaker on December 21 at the Lapu-lapu Grandstand.<br /><br />The beginning of the anniversary program was marked by a high-speed opener featuring the AFP's two FA-50 fighter aircraft and a parade featuring contingents coming from the AFP's different branches of service.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/DECEMBER%202023/GB5-IO8bEAAfIb_.jpg","image_caption":"The Chief of Staff, Armed Forces of the Philippines, General Romeo S Brawner Jr. PA accompanies the Commander-in-Chief, AFP, President Ferdinand R Marcos Jr. in inspecting the troops during the 88th AFP Anniversary Celebration on December 21, 2023 at the Lapu-lapu Grandstand.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-01-21T20:15:40+08:00","hits":2011},{"id":601,"title":"AFP PREPARES FOR 88TH ANNIVERSARY RITES","slug":"afp-prepares-for-88th-anniversary-rites","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City--The Armed Forces of the Philippines is all set in the celebration of its 88th anniversary of December 21 that will culminate in the parade and program with the Commander-in-Chief, President Ferdinand Marcos Jr, as guest of honor and speaker.<br /><br /></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs xtlvy1s x126k92a\">\r\n<div dir=\"auto\">A series of activities were held leading up to the anniversary proper, including the Simultaneous Wreath-Laying Ceremony and anniversary concert on December 15, Talakayang Mabini 2023: Policy and Strategic Studies Forum last November 27, and Anniversary Fun Run on December 7, among others.","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2023/DECEMBER%202023/AFP%20PREPARES%20FOR%2088TH%20ANNIVERSARY%20RITES.jpg","image_caption":"A division-size parading element is among the highlights of the 88th AFP Anniversary program and parade on December 21 at the Lapu-Lapu Grandstand in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-01-20T17:00:21+08:00","hits":1809},{"id":602,"title":"AFP renders honors to Police LtGen Sermonia","slug":"afp-renders-honors-to-police-ltgen-sermonia","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City--The Armed Forces of the Philippines rendered arrival honors to PLtGen Rhodel Sermonia, the Deputy Chief for Administration of the Philippine National Police, during his exit call to the Chief of Staff AFP on January 17 at the General Headquarters here.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/January%202024/pnp.jpg","image_caption":"General Romeo Brawner Jr, the Chief of Staff AFP, receives PLtGen Rhodel Sermonia, the Deputy Chief for Administration of the Philippine National Police, during the latter’s exit call in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City on January 17.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-01-18T08:54:32+08:00","hits":2855},{"id":603,"title":"AFP reactivates Counterintelligence Group","slug":"afp-reactivates-counterintelligence-group","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – Fueled by the commitment of the Commander-in-Chief to secure the nation, the Chief of Staff, Armed Forces of the Philippines (CSAFP), General Romeo S Brawner Jr PA led the reactivation of the AFP Counterintelligence Group (AFPCIG) in a ceremony conducted on January 18 at the General Headquarters. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/January%202024/ci.jpg","image_caption":"The Chief of Staff, Armed Forces of the Philippines, General Romeo S Brawner Jr PA, hands over the Office Symbol to the Acting Commander of the AFP Counterintelligence Group (AFPCIG), Col. Jonathan Manio PA, during the Reactivation Ceremony of the AFPCIG, on January 18, 2024 in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-01-18T08:52:08+08:00","hits":3004},{"id":604,"title":"AFP, AFPSLAI conduct Blessing and Ceremonial Handover of Modular Transient Facility","slug":"afp-afpslai-conduct-blessing-and-ceremonial-handover-of-modular-transient-facility","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p>CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Deputy Chief of Staff, Armed Forces of the Philippines (TDCSAFP), LtGen Charlton Sean M Gaerlan PN(M), led the Blessing and Ceremonial Handover of One (1) Cluster 2-Storey Modular Transient Facility donated by the Armed Forces and Police Savings and Loans Association, Inc. (AFPSLAI) in a ceremony conducted on January 17 here at the General Headquarters. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/January%202024/lai.jpg","image_caption":"The Deputy Chief of Staff, Armed Forces of the Philippines (TDCSAFP), LtGen Charlton Sean M Gaerlan PN(M), poses for a photo with AFPSLAI President and CEO, VAdm Gaudencio Collado Jr PN (Ret) during the Blessing and Ceremonial Handover of One Cluster 2-Storey Modular Transient Facility Room donated by the Armed Forces and Police Savings and Loans Association, Inc. (AFPSLAI) on January 17, 2024 in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-01-17T08:35:36+08:00","hits":1779},{"id":605,"title":"AFP Chief, Major Service Commanders visit Malacañang","slug":"afp-chief-major-service-commanders-visit-malacanang","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, and the commanders of the Major Services visited Malacañan Palace on Wednesday, January 17 for the New Year’s Call to President Ferdinand Marcos Jr.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The AFP Chief was joined by LtGen Roy Galido, Commanding General of the Philippine Army; LtGen Stephen Parreño, Commanding General of the Philippine Air Force; and VAdm Toribio Adaci Jr, Flag Officer in Command of the Philippine Navy. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/January%202024/NYC2.jpg","image_caption":"President Ferdinand Marcos Jr and Presidential Adviser on Police and Military Affairs Secretary Roman Felix pose for a photo with General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines; LtGen Roy Galido, Commanding General of the Philippine Army; LtGen Stephen Parreño, Commanding General of the Philippine Air Force; and VAdm Toribio Adaci Jr, Flag Officer in Command of the Philippine Navy; during the New Year’s Call at Malacañan Palace on January 17.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-01-17T08:33:09+08:00","hits":2084},{"id":606,"title":"AFP Commander-in-Chief lauds outstanding units for dismantling Guerilla Fronts","slug":"afp-commander-in-chief-lauds-outstanding-units-for-dismantling-guerilla-fronts","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City – The Commander-in-Chief, Armed Forces of the Philippines, President Ferdinand R Marcos Jr, led the awarding of the Campaign Streamer awards to outstanding military units during the Year-End 2023 Command Conference conducted on January 15 at the General Headquarters.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/January%202024/ban.jpg","image_caption":"AFP Commander-in-Chief, President Ferdinand R Marcos Jr., attaches the campaign streamers awarded to the 801Bde, 8ID, PA, received by BGen Lenart R Lelina PA, during the Command Conference conducted on January 15, 2024, in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.  (Photo by Mr Fred Abuda Jr, DND)","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-01-15T08:43:44+08:00","hits":1626},{"id":607,"title":"AFP conducts command conference with President Marcos Jr","slug":"afp-conducts-command-conference-with-president-marcos-jr","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Armed Forces of the Philippines held its yearend Command Conference on January 15 with the Commander in Chief, President Ferdinand Marcos Jr, in attendance to hear updates on the AFP’s campaigns and programs and deliver his guidance.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the AFP, led top military officers from the General Headquarters, AFP-wide Support and Separate Units, Major Services, and Unified Commands, and commanders of the army, air force, and naval units on the ground.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/January%202024/CC3.jpg","image_caption":"President Ferdinand Marcos Jr leads the AFP Command Conference on January 15 in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City. He was joined by the Executive Secretary Lucas Bersamin, Special Assistant to the President Antonio Lagdameo Jr, Secretary of National Defense Gilbert Teodoro Jr, and AFP Chief of Staff General Romeo Brawner Jr.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-01-15T08:41:20+08:00","hits":2292},{"id":608,"title":"Gen. Brawner graces Ihudyat Concert 2024","slug":"gen-brawner-graces-ihudyat-concert-2024","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City — The Chief of Staff, Armed Forces of the Philippines, General Romeo S Brawner Jr. PA served as the Guest of Honor and Speaker during the Ihudyat Concert 2024 on January 13 conducted at the AFP Commissioned Officers Country. </p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In his message, Gen. Brawner emphasized the rich history, traditions and impact of the University of the Philippines (UP) Reserve Officers' Training Corps (ROTC) and its contributions to serving the country. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/January%202024/IC1.jpg","image_caption":"The Chief of Staff, Armed Forces of the Philippines, General Romeo S Brawner Jr. PA,  delivers his message during the Ihudyat 2024 on January 13, 2024 in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-01-15T08:39:14+08:00","hits":1226},{"id":609,"title":"CSAFP dons ranks to 8 newly promoted military officers","slug":"csafp-dons-ranks-to-8-newly-promoted-military-officers","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, General Romeo Brawner Jr, donned higher ranks to eight newly promoted military officers in a ceremony held on January 12 at the AFP General Headquarters here.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/January%202024/don1.jpg","image_caption":"General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, dons new ranks on MGen Edmundo G Peralta during the donning of ranks ceremony for newly promoted officers on January 12 in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-01-12T16:15:14+08:00","hits":3822},{"id":610,"title":"AFP conducts 1st GFPS EXECOM meeting in 2024","slug":"afp-conducts-1st-gfps-execom-meeting-in-2024","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City—The Armed Forces of the Philippines’ Gender and Development (GAD) Focal Point System (AFPGFPS) Executive Committee (EXECOM) held its first meeting in 2024 on January 11 at the AFP General Headquarters here. </p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/January%202024/exe1.jpg","image_caption":"The AFP Vice Chief of Staff, LtGen Arthur Cordura, presides over the Gender and Development Focal Point System Executive Committee Meeting on January 11 at the AFP General Headquarters in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-01-12T08:42:59+08:00","hits":751},{"id":611,"title":"DND, AFP hold Joint New Year’s Call","slug":"dnd-afp-hold-joint-new-year-s-call","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">CAMP AGUINALDO, Quezon City--The Department of National Defense and the Armed Forces of the Philippines held their traditional New Year’s Call led by Defense Secretary Gilbert Teodoro Jr and AFP Chief of Staff General Romeo Brawner Jr on January 12 here.</p>\r\n","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/January%202024/nc7.jpg","image_caption":"Secretary of National Defense Gilbert Teodoro Jr welcomes General Romeo Brawner, Chief of Staff of the Armed Forces of the Philippines, to the Joint Department of National Defense-Armed Forces of the Philippines New Year's Call on January 12 in Camp Aguinaldo, Quezon City.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-01-12T08:41:15+08:00","hits":869},{"id":612,"title":"Mensahe ni General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff Armed Forces of the Philippines, sa pagdiriwang ng pista ng Itim na Nazareno sa ika-9 ng Enero 2024.","slug":"mensahe-ni-general-romeo-brawner-jr-chief-of-staff-armed-forces-of-the-philippines-sa-pagdiriwang-ng-pista-ng-itim-na-nazareno-sa-ika-9-ng-enero-2024","category":7,"category_name":"News Blog","category_slug":"news-blog","intro_html":"","featured_image":"/media/legacy/images/Articles/2024/January%202024/naz%201.jpg","image_caption":"Mensahe ni General Romeo Brawner Jr, Chief of Staff Armed Forces of the Philippines, sa pagdiriwang ng pista ng Itim na Nazareno sa ika-9 ng Enero 2024.","is_featured":false,"published_at":"2024-01-08T14:41:55+08:00","hits":427}]}